    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0401" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg359"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By telegraph.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 15, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Port Hudson unconditionally surrendered on
                    the 9th of July. Bragg is reported to be retreating from Chattanooga. Lee is
                    retiring from the Potomac. The movement at Charleston has begun favorably.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
